    // only the keys it changes (boardUpdateOk: diff().affectedKeys()). Measured on the emulator with the seeded
    // boards and a board at every cap (test/rules/pizarra-budget.test.ts; impl/SERVIDOR.txt has the numbers).
    // Content beyond these caps (each drawing, jugada, step…) is validated on read (lineupDoc.ts, Zod).
    // r14 · el plan (PZ-D22P/D23P): the keys (≤ 3 texts of 1–60, joined by «¬» and split back: the same list), each
    // one's light on the pitch (`viz`, ≤ 3 maps { icon, zona }: two strings — the «+» refuses anything else — of
    // ≤ 24 together), the notes for the charla (≤ 400) and the set pieces (`parado`: corners / freekicks
    // { playId: null or ≤ 128, box }, penalties { rechace }; every player id of the three lists in ONE idListOk,
    // ≤ 5 per list). Its content is validated on read (data/plan.ts). Lean for the budget (see boardFieldsOk).
    // A list of at most `max` player ids (id characters, «guest:g1» too; ≤ 129 per id on average, each ≤ 128 on read),
    // checked in one regex; splitting the joined
